  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical moving coil galvanometer have <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistance and full scale deflection at <math><mn>2</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> current. One of them is converted into a voltmeter of <math><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> full scale reading and the other into an Ammeter of <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> full scale current using appropriate resistors. These are then used to measure the voltage and current in the Ohm&#39;s law experiment with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistor by using an ideal cell. Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bn9g2",
      "text": "The resistance of the Voltmeter will be  <math><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>.</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tLmCe",
      "text": "The measured value of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>  will be  <math><mn>978</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>982</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>.</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
